; ART_BIBLE.md section 5: no ceilings -- every room is "open to a soft cream
; void". Section 7: high warm ambient fill, which is the only thing that stops
; the dark side of a form going muddy under a single directional light, and
; permanently mid-morning.
;
; Nothing is enabled here that section 7 forbids: no GI/SDFGI/VoxelGI, no SSAO,
; no SSIL, no SSR, no glow, no volumetric fog, no depth of field, no colour
; correction. Every one of those is off by default and must stay off.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; These four numbers, and the light below them, are the SAME values held as
; constants in `scripts/house/lighting.gd::AFTER`, with the reasoning for each
; written out there and in `docs/LIGHTING_PASS.md`. They are duplicated on
; purpose -- the scene must look right in the editor without a script running --
; and `tests/cases/test_lighting_house.gd` fails if the two copies ever drift.
;
; Ambient is 0.62 -> 0.52 and is no longer `cream`: `cream` fill on `cream`
; walls can only ever produce more cream, which is the "milky" look stated as a
; colour identity. It is now CREAM -> PEACH at 0.35 (#FFEAD5), which is section
; 3's "never darken by value alone, always mix toward `ink`" -- so the shaded
; side of every form goes warm instead of going pale.
;
; The background is deeper too. As the brightest thing in frame it made the room
; read as a cut-out held up in front of a light box.
[sub_resource type="Environment" id="Environment_house"]
background_mode = 1
tonemap_mode = 0
background_color = Color(0.8958, 0.852, 0.7814, 1)
ambient_light_source = 2
ambient_light_color = Color(1, 0.9167, 0.8336, 1)
ambient_light_energy = 0.52

[sub_resource type="CapsuleShape3D" id="CapsuleShape3D_buddy"]
radius = 0.22
height = 1.5

[node name="HouseWorld" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1")

[node name="WorldEnvironment" type="WorldEnvironment" parent="."]
environment = SubResource("Environment_house")

; Exactly one, and never more (section 7, non-negotiable; `test_house_world.gd`
; pins the count).
;
; ## The sun was under the floor, and had been since this scene was authored
;
; `Transform3D(...)` takes its nine basis values in ROW-major order, and the
; matrix that used to be here --
;   Transform3D(0.7826, 0, 0.6225, 0.4769, 0.6428, -0.5995, -0.4001, 0.766, 0.5031, ...)
; -- was written as though they were the x, y and z AXES, i.e. columns. The
; transpose of a rotation is another perfectly valid rotation, so nothing
; errored and nothing warned. Read back live off the running light, the house
; was lit from (0.623, -0.599, 0.503): elevation -36.8 degrees, azimuth +51.1 --
; a sun BELOW the floor, shining upwards. The comment that used to sit here
; ("mid-morning sun from the upper left, rotation (-50, -34, 0)") described a
; light this file did not contain, and `WORLD_POLISH_PASS.md` section 8 and the
; towel note in `house_layout.gd` both read the same matrix the same wrong way.
;
; Every upward-facing surface in the house -- floor, worktop, table, bed, sill,
; and the top of every head -- therefore received ZERO key light and sat at flat
; ambient, while every downward-facing one got the full key. That is the whole
; of the "milky, no depth, nothing has weight" complaint.
;
; This is elevation 48, azimuth +61, written out the way the constructor really
; reads it (rows). `scripts/house/lighting.gd` states the same rotation as two
; angles, and `tests/cases/test_lighting_house.gd` fails if this matrix stops
; agreeing with them -- including if it is ever transposed again.
;
; Azimuth stays POSITIVE, so the sun stays on the side it has always appeared to
; be on and no room's composition flips: the `-X` wall (screen left, the one the
; bathroom towel hangs on) is the lit one, the `+X` wall sits at pure ambient,
; and the back wall lands between them. Three walls, three values.
;
; Key energy 1.12 -> 0.61 is exposure, not mood. With the sun under the floor
; only two planes caught it and both clipped; lift it and five times as much
; surface catches it, so the old energy would have blown the room out. 24.5% of
; the kitchen frame used to sit at or above 0.97 luminance. It is now 0.1%.
;
; Shadows stay OFF (section 7 amendment, 2026-09-18, owner decision taken on a
; physical iPhone). Nothing in this pass re-enables them: the settings below are
; kept, unchanged and inert, exactly as that amendment asks.
[node name="DirectionalLight3D" type="DirectionalLight3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(0.48481, -0.649971, 0.585237, 0, 0.669131, 0.743145, -0.87462, -0.36028, 0.324398, 0, 6, 3)
light_color = Color(1, 0.93464, 0.85752, 1)
light_energy = 0.61
light_angular_distance = 2.4
shadow_enabled = false
shadow_bias = 0.06
shadow_normal_bias = 0.6
shadow_opacity = 0.72
shadow_blur = 1.2
directional_shadow_mode = 0
directional_shadow_max_distance = 9.0

